PRETABLE_6 -- mvme187memcoob detector, test-variant table 6 (repair 6: session R18, 213 rows).  Written BEFORE table 6 runs
(this file's mtime precedes table6/SCORES.txt).  Instrument: table6/probe213_frozen.py, copied from regress/mvme187_memc_probe.py
after the R18 edit (md5 1d69cc4e6cb1499894fdf1fcbe3049bd); base on the clone's restored baseline binary 213/213,
r7_20261105/base213/probe_base213.out.  Baseline: GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_mvme187.c (repair 6 changes the probe, not the
device).  STEP 1 (before any probe edit): the eight own-latch variants measured 206/206 on the 206-row probe in a fresh clone,
base 206/206 (r7_20261105/step1/SCORES.txt, step1/FRESHNESS.txt).  Legs first, in one fresh clone: base, HEAD
(det_20261104/dev_mvme187.c.HEAD), three null media, B1-B3; then the eight; then the other 657 of table 5's 665 green
representatives (`memc_variants_5.py apply`).

METHOD.  Every `exact` prediction is the frozen 213-row probe's own verdict on memc_variants_5.py's device model (class Device,
the fake gxemul: the probe's m88k words run against DEVICE_ACCESS(mvme187_memc) as written in the fix, with the variant's
statement inserted).  The eight are also walked by hand below.  B3 is not a statement the model expresses: its prediction
is table 5's measured set, carried (reason under LEGS).

CALIBRATION (the model on table 5's frozen 206-row instrument against table 5's MEASURED SCORES.txt): 0 mismatches
   base               MATCH
   HEAD               MATCH
   null_true          MATCH
   null_absent        MATCH
   null_false         MATCH
   B1_cnf_exit        MATCH
   B2_def_exit        MATCH
   the 665 green representatives: 665 of 665 modelled green on the 206 rows (measured: 665 green)

THE FOUR CHECKS for R18's seven rows (mandatory: repair 6 extends a kill-table-backed detector):
  SIBLING PARITY -- R18 is one session with two arms, default (+0x18) then memconf (+0x08), each given the same three stores
    (0x01, 0x01, 0x00) and one load; each arm has a notice row naming the first value, a readback row, and shares lines/pc.
  CLAIM -> ROW -- 'one announce per category' -> R18 lines; 'the first store of each category is announced with its value' ->
    R18 def line, R18 cnf line; 'memconf keeps no store' -> R18 08 r4 (3 after 0x01, 0x01, 0x00); 'the accesses retire' ->
    R18 pc; 'the session survives' -> R18 session.  R18 18 r2 reads 0 after the default stores, but its last store is 0x00,
    so it is not a keep detector for the default arm (R5's and R10's readbacks carry that claim).
  GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the memconf guard reads writeflag and warned_memconf (dev_mvme187.c:105, :112); its body reads
    idata and controller and sets warned_memconf (:113-116).  The default guard reads warned_default (:127); its body reads
    writeflag, relative_addr, controller and idata and sets warned_default (:128-135).  The eight write the guard's own field
    from the arm that reads it.  `^= idata` takes a latch of 1 to zero only on idata 0x01; `= idata` takes it to zero on
    0x00.  The 206 rows make no store of 0x01 in any arm and no non-first default store of 0x00 (step 1 measured the eight
    green there); R18 makes 0x01 stores (first and second) and a non-first 0x00 store in both arms.
  CHANNEL (row: the variant it is built to kill -> the observable that differs):
    R18 lines    -- each of the eight -> the announce count (4 for the four ungated toggles, 3 for the other four).
    R18 def line -- the default notice's value guard or direction gated off for this store -> the fragment
                    'unimplemented write to offset 0x18 (controller 0): 0x1 (once) ]' is absent.
    R18 cnf line -- the memconf notice gated off for 0x01 -> 'memconf write 0x1 (controller 0) ignored, not modelled (once) ]'
                    is absent.
    R18 18 r2    -- an exit at any R18 access (HEAD, B1, B2) -> no register dump, r2 reads 'none'.
    R18 08 r4    -- a memconf keep that one of R18's three memconf stores changes -> memconf reads other than 0x3.
    R18 pc       -- an exit (no register dump: 'none') or a fault at any of the eight accesses -> pc is not CODE + 32.
    R18 session  -- an exit (HEAD, B1, B2) -> exit1.

THE EIGHT (step 1: each 206/206 on the 206 rows).  Predicted red on 213 rows -- the model's exact set, then the hand walk:
   L_MB_M_xori_any    exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 4)
                        MB runs only when the memconf notice fires.  1st 0x01: announce, M = 1, M ^= 1 -> 0.  2nd 0x01: M == 0,
                        announce, M = 1 -> 0.  3rd 0x00: announce, M = 1, M ^= 0 -> 1.  Memconf notices 3, default 1: lines 4.
   L_ME_M_xori_any    exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 4)
                        ME runs on every memconf access.  1st 0x01: announce, M = 1, ME -> 0.  2nd 0x01: announce, M = 1 -> 0.
                        3rd 0x00: announce, M = 1, ^ 0 -> 1.  Load: ^ 0.  Memconf notices 3, default 1: lines 4.
   L_DB_D_xori_any    exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 4)
                        DB runs only when the default notice fires.  1st 0x01: announce, D = 1, D ^= 1 -> 0.  2nd 0x01: announce,
                        D = 1 -> 0.  3rd 0x00: announce, D = 1, ^ 0 -> 1.  Load: D == 1, silent.  Default 3, memconf 1: lines 4.
   L_DA_D_xori_any    exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 4)
                        DA runs on every default access.  1st 0x01: announce, D = 1, DA -> 0.  2nd 0x01: announce, D = 1 -> 0.
                        3rd 0x00: announce, D = 1, ^ 0 -> 1.  Load: silent, ^ 0.  Default 3, memconf 1: lines 4.
   L_MT_M_xori_M      exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 3)
                        MT runs on every memconf access before the write block, gated on M.  1st 0x01: M == 0, no toggle; announce,
                        M = 1.  2nd 0x01: M ^= 1 -> 0, then announce, M = 1.  3rd 0x00: M ^= 0 -> 1, silent.  Load: ^ 0.  Lines 3.
   L_MW_M_xori_M      exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 3)
                        MW runs on every memconf store before the latch test, gated on M.  1st 0x01: no toggle; announce, M = 1.
                        2nd 0x01: M -> 0, announce, M = 1.  3rd 0x00: M ^= 0 -> 1, silent.  Lines 3.
   L_DT_D_xori_D      exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 3)
                        DT runs on every default access before the latch test, gated on D.  1st 0x01: no toggle; announce, D = 1.
                        2nd 0x01: D -> 0, announce, D = 1.  3rd 0x00: D ^= 0 -> 1, silent.  Load: ^ 0, silent.  Lines 3.
   L_DT_D_idat_W.D    exact: R18_lines   (R18 lines: 3)
                        DT, gated on a store with D set.  1st 0x01: D == 0, no assign; announce, D = 1.  2nd 0x01: D = 1.
                        3rd 0x00: D = 0, then announce (': 0x0'), D = 1.  Load: not a store, silent.  Lines 3.

